2026-10-27 00:56:16+07:00 [INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:215] 2026-10-26 17:56:16,409 >> Wait, when you add vectors, the magnitude of their sum depends on the angle between them. Oh right, the formula for the magnitude of the sum is |a + b| = sqrt( ||a||² + ||b||² + 2||a|| ||b|| cosθ ), where θ is the angle between them. So, to minimize this, I need to find the minimum value of this expression with respect to θ.
2026-10-27 00:56:16+07:00 [INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:215] 2026-10-26 17:56:16,409 >> 
2026-10-27 00:56:16+07:00 [INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:215] 2026-10-26 17:56:16,409 >> So, the expression inside the square root is |a|² + |b|² + 2|a||b|cosθ. Since |a| is 3 and |b| is 14, let's plug those numbers in. That becomes 3² + 14² + 2*3*14*cosθ. Which simplifies to 9 + 196 + 84 cosθ, so 205 + 84 cosθ.
2026-10-27 00:56:16+07:00 [INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:215] 2026-10-26 17:56:16,409 >> 
2026-10-27 00:56:16+07:00 [INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:215] 2026-10-26 17:56:16,409 >> Wait, so to minimize |a + b|, I need to minimize the square root of (205 + 84 cosθ). Since the square root is a monotonically increasing function, the minimum of the square root occurs at the minimum of the expression inside. So, the expression inside is 205 + 84 cosθ. What's the smallest this can be?
2026-10-27 00:56:16+07:00 [INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:215] 2026-10-26 17:56:16,409 >> 
2026-10-27 00:56:16+07:00 [INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:215] 2026-10-26 17:56:16,409 >> Well, the cosine of θ ranges from -1 to 1. So, the minimum value of cosθ is -1, and the maximum is 1. So, if I plug cosθ = -1 into the expression, 205 + 84*(-1) = 205 - 84 = 121. So the expression inside the square root becomes 121, and the square root of 121 is 11. So, the minimal value is 11.
