2026-10-27 00:56:39+07:00 [INFO|on_policy_episode_generator.py:149:215] 2026-10-26 17:56:39,571 >>     "gold_solution_steps_str": "We are given \\[f(x) + 2f \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right) = 3x.\\]\nReplacing $x$ with $\\frac{1}{x},$ we get\n\\[f \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right) + 2f(x) = \\frac{3}{x}.\\]\nWe can view these equations as a system in $f(x)$ and $f \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right).$\nSolving for $f(x),$ we find\n\\[f(x) = \\frac{2 - x^2}{x}.\\]\nThen the equation $f(x) = f(-x)$ becomes\n\\[\\frac{2 - x^2}{x} = \\frac{2 - x^2}{-x}.\\]\nThen $2 - x^2 = x^2 - 2,$ so $x^2 = 2.$\nThe solutions are $\\boxed{\\sqrt{2},-\\sqrt{2}}.$",
