2026-10-27 01:02:58+07:00 [INFO|base_episode_generator.py:177:3173] 2026-10-26 18:02:58,110 >> First, I remember that probability problems like this often involve combinations because the order doesn't matter. So, I should calculate the number of favorable outcomes divided by the total number of possible outcomes.
2026-10-27 01:02:58+07:00 [INFO|base_episode_generator.py:177:3173] 2026-10-26 18:02:58,110 >> 
2026-10-27 01:02:58+07:00 [INFO|base_episode_generator.py:177:3173] 2026-10-26 18:02:58,110 >> The total number of ways to choose 2 people out of 20 is the combination of 20 choose 2. The formula for combinations is n choose k = n! / (k! * (n - k)!), where n is the total number and k is the number we're choosing. So for 20 choose 2, that would be 20! / (2! * 18!) which simplifies to (20 * 19)/2 = 190. So there are 190 possible pairs.
